On 19.02.2013 18:53, Gerhard Strangar wrote:
> High,
> 
> I recently found this game in the FreeBSD ports collection and I think I
> understood the basics. But there's somthing I'm not sure about:
> Do you ascend by strategy or by incident?

By strategy and tactics. But since there's the mighty RNG there's also
random incidents that may favour one game over another. But on average a
whole game won't be influenced by many lucky incidents so much, compared
to a sophisticated play. (Well, some will correctly say that a lucky
early found wand of wishing will indeed make it a lot simpler - but a
newbie will likely die anyway at some point due to lack of experience.)

> If it's not strategy, how can someone do serveral ascensions in a row?

To ascend on a regular basis you need to build up knowledge about the
game; that needs time. Then there's a couple standard situations that
you can solve by tactical experience, or by watching how others play;
have a look at the NAO server to view actual games of other players.
(See http://alt.org/nethack and/or telnet to nethack.alt.org)

> Do successful players need to do lots of repetitive moves, like making
> you pet get everying from the shop to get items or create and kill
> monsters to gain levels?

Well, partly. There might be instances where you want the whole loot
of a shop and have no money. In other games you might not have enough
food to eat, so you strive towards the places where you find something
before you get in danger to starve. But some places are dangerous, so
you need to obtain good armour and a good weapon. Wimpy characters may
try to keep their pet alive since their life depends on him fighting
monsters for you. In one sentence; the game has a lot balanced variety
that allows you to choose how to play. There's not one way how to win,
but you will find out that there's many ways to die. :-)

Happy Nethacking!

